onsistency} +?For the preceding construction, $\|\Psi\|=\|\psi\|$. For arbitrary +?operators $A$ on $\mathcal H_A$ and $B$ on $\mathcal H_B$, +?\[ +??\operatorname{Re}\langle\Psi, +?? ((A\otimes\Id)\otimes(\Id\otimes B))\Psi\rangle +??=\operatorname{Re}\langle\psi,(A\otimes B)\psi\rangle. +?\] +?Consequently every averaged off-diagonal consistency defect is preserved +?by these local placements, for arbitrary operator families and any finite +?distribution. Positivity and state normalization are not required. +\end{lemma} +\begin{proof} +?\leanok +?\uses{def:pasting-product-state} +?Expand the norm and quadratic form in the standard bases. The fixed +?coordinates remove two sums. Sum the quadratic-form identity over unequal +?answers and average over the question distribution. +\end{proof} + +\begin{lemma}[Pasting on independent local spaces] +?\label{lem:pasting-heterogeneous} +?\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_pasting_error_heterogeneous} +?\leanok +?\uses{def:consistency, def:bracket, def:povm-conventions} +?There is a universal function +?$\delta_{\mathrm{pasting}}(\eta,\delta)=\poly(\eta,\delta)$ for which +?Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons} holds with independent finite +?local spaces $\mathcal H_A$ and $\mathcal H_B$. The family $A$ acts on +?$\mathcal H_A$, the families $G_1,G_2$ act on $\mathcal H_B$, and the +?unit state belongs to $\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B$. All conditional +?collision, projectivity, and forward comparison hypotheses, and the +?conclusion~\eqref{eq:pasting-3}, are retained. This is a +?formalization-only strengthening of Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting}. +\end{lemma} +\begin{proof} +?\leanok +?\uses{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons, lem:pasting-product-state-preservation, +??lem:pasting-tensor-placement} +?A unit state implies that both local spaces are nonzero. Choose one basis +?vector in each and adjoin them as in Definition~\ref{def:pasting-product-state}. +?The common local space is $\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B$. +?Tensor placement preserves projectivity, postprocessing, and the product +?$G_2G_1G_2$. Both input defects and the pasted output defect are unchanged. +?Apply Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons} on this common space. +\end{proof} +  \begin{lemma}[Universal bound for placed consistency defects]  ?\label{lem:pasting-defect-bound}  ?\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_placed_le_one} diff --git a/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex b/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex index 14663773..a2ce5476 100644 --- a/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex +++ b/blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex @@ -956,6 +956,33 @@ assembled by Fourier averaging.    \section{Combined line measurements}   +\begin{lemma}[Formalization support for coefficient polynomial agreement] +?\label{lem:coefficient-polynomial-agreement} +?\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.evalCoefficient_collision_card_le} +?\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.linePolynomialOfCoefficients_eq_ofFn, +??MIPStarRE.QPBT.linePolynomialOfCoefficients_eval, +??MIPStarRE.QPBT.linePolynomialOfCoefficients_injective, +??MIPStarRE.QPBT.linePolynomialOfCoefficients_natDegree_le} +?\leanok +?Let $K$ be a finite integral domain, let $c\in\N$, and let +?$f,g\in K^{c+1}$ be distinct coefficient vectors. Their polynomials +?$p_f(T)=\sum_{i=0}^{c}f_iT^i$ and $p_g(T)=\sum_{i=0}^{c}g_iT^i$ +?agree at at most $c$ elements of $K$. +?The coefficient representation is injective, preserves evaluation, +?and has natural degree  <<<END-UNTRUSTED-DATA>>> (truncated by the aggregate 100000-byte attachment cap; full file: /home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr483/acdda3ff9a89887de4630c7a9e308ad39bd06a2c/diff.sanitized.txt)  <<<UNTRUSTED-DATA name="prior-ledger.md">>>  <<<END-UNTRUSTED-DATA>>> (truncated by the aggregate 100000-byte attachment cap; full file: /home/drx/.cache/mipstarre-dev/reviews/pr483/acdda3ff9a89887de4630c7a9e308ad39bd06a2c/prior-ledger.md)  # Task  # Review task (trusted, read from committed main)  The section below is .gith