1234		Use coordinate indices $i\in\{0,\dots,m-1\}$ throughout this definition,
1235		the following mixture estimates, and the sub-line construction below. Write
1236		$\bar\chi(s)=\chi(s)-1$, where $\chi$ is the one-based index function of
1237		Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}. Thus $\bar\chi$ takes
1238		values in $\{0,\dots,m-1\}$, and index $i$ here denotes coordinate $i+1$
1239		in the one-based notation of \cite{Ji2020MIPStar}.
1240		For any such $i$, the \emph{$i$-th restricted
1241		axis-parallel line distribution} $D_{\mathrm{ALine},i}$ is the
1242		restriction of $D_{\mathrm{ALine}}$ to pairs $(\ell, u)$ where the line
1243		$\ell$ is along the direction $e_i$, i.e.\ is of the form
1244		$\ell = (u_0, e_i)$. Similarly, the \emph{$i$-th restricted diagonal line
1245		distribution} $D_{\mathrm{DLine},i}$ is the restriction of
1246		$D_{\mathrm{DLine}}$ to pairs $(\ell, u)$ where the line
1247		$\ell = (u_0, s, v)$ satisfies $\bar\chi(s) = i$ and coordinates
1248		$0, \dots, i-1$ of $v$ are $0$, with no such coordinates when $i=0$.
1249	\end{definition}
